# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
# dist IS committed: the event runs offline, and gb10_bootstrap.sh clones the
# repo bundle onto a machine with no npm registry. Without a committed dist,
# meety_api mounts nothing and the console 404s at "/" (hit for real on
# 2026-07-26). Rebuild with `npm run build` and commit the result.
#
# A developer's GLOBAL gitignore very often carries a blanket `dist/`, which
# silently swallows the freshly-hashed bundle: the old assets show up deleted,
# the new ones never appear as untracked, and the commit ships a dist that
# points at files which no longer exist. Repo rules beat the global file, so
# re-include it here — directory first, because git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
!dist/
!dist/**
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
